		{ ref: `Romans 8:15`, slug: `romans`, ch: 8, text: `You did not receive a spirit of slavery, to fall back into fear, but received the Spirit of sonship, by whom we cry, "Abba! Father!"`, note: `If faith was handed to you as fear, this says fear was never the point — belonging was.` },
		{ ref: `1 John 3:1`, slug: `1-john`, ch: 3, text: `See what kind of love our Father has given us, that we should be called children of our Father! And we are. The world doesn't know us because it didn't know him.`, note: `Not earned, not conditional. Just given. You're allowed to be skeptical of that — and still curious about it.` },
